  "body": "The URL standard says \"A URL is a universal identifier. To disambiguate from a URL string it can also be referred to as a URL record.\" So it's not correct to refer to this definition of \"URL\" for the validity requirements of an href attribute, which contains a string, not a record. I assume it was intended to refer to a \"URL string\", which is (more or less) the valid input to the URL parser.",
